# What the kind end-to-end test installs, pinned (09 acceptance 3; S19). Read with `. deploy/tests/kind/pins.env`. Every value was
# READ from the registry or the release on 2026-10-26, never guessed, and each was published at least 14 days before.
#
# The node image: Kubernetes v1.37.0 as kind v0.33.0 ships it (the default image that the pinned kind binary names, `strings kind |
# grep kindest/node`). The digest is the index digest, equal to `crane digest kindest/node:v1.37.0` on Docker Hub; the amd64 image
# was built 2026-08-26. The image holds kubectl (run.sh drives the cluster with it, so the client is the cluster's version), crictl
# and containerd 2.3.4, and, as every kind node image does, the control plane's images, the CNI (kindnet) and the storage provisioner.
# It needs cgroup v2 on the host: its kubelet refuses to run on cgroup v1 (run.sh checks).
LK_KIND_NODE_IMAGE=kindest/node:v1.37.0@sha256:a1ed56cfb0e7b93589bdf97c8cd566405a265939e3620fc4f5de89adff580ae5
# CloudNativePG 1.30.1, the operator whose CRDs deploy/schemas holds (tag v1.30.1, commit date 2026-09-23). The manifest is the
# release's own file; run.sh checks its sha256 (computed from the download of 2026-10-26, 1,293,413 bytes) before it applies a byte, and
# then names the operator image by digest (the index digest, `crane digest ghcr.io/cloudnative-pg/cloudnative-pg:1.30.1`).
LK_CNPG_VERSION=1.30.1
LK_CNPG_MANIFEST_URL=https://github.com/cloudnative-pg/cloudnative-pg/releases/download/v1.30.1/cnpg-1.30.1.yaml
LK_CNPG_MANIFEST_SHA256=37237f145d8138256ea25ae830f87759255665ff08f8d552fdd8224a5ec032fb
LK_CNPG_OPERATOR_IMAGE=ghcr.io/cloudnative-pg/cloudnative-pg:1.30.1@sha256:923c267ec29636db3bee20f993d0ec4973fa22998e1adad37da79e4d32b5bc07
